# ─── Supabase (radar project) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project URL, e.g. https://ceramicaapp-9abd8.supabase.co  (no trailing slash).
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co

# Service-role key (server-side only — bypasses RLS). Treat as a secret.
# Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API → service_role key.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...

# ─── Jetstream (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Full WebSocket URL of the Bluesky Jetstream instance to subscribe to.
# Optional: the worker defaults to jetstream2.us-east and appends
# ?wantedCollections=app.bsky.feed.post itself, so leave unset unless you want
# to pin a different instance. If you set it WITHOUT a wantedCollections query
# param, the worker adds it; if you include your own query string, it is used
# as-is. Public instances:
#   wss://jetstream1.us-east.bsky.network/subscribe
#   wss://jetstream2.us-east.bsky.network/subscribe
#   wss://jetstream1.us-west.bsky.network/subscribe
#   wss://jetstream2.us-west.bsky.network/subscribe
# JETSTREAM_URL=wss://jetstream2.us-east.bsky.network/subscribe

# ─── atproto API host (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Host used to resolve a DID → handle (com.atproto.repo.describeRepo), without
# auth. Defaults to https://api.bsky.app (public.api.bsky.app is blocked at the
# CDN for some endpoints — see lib/sources/bluesky.ts). No trailing slash.
# ATPROTO_API_URL=https://api.bsky.app
